  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Given that $P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],$ find $det(P).$",
  "worked_solution": "Given two $n\\times n$ matrices $M$ and $N,$ we have\n\n$$\ndet(MN)=det(M)\\cdot det(N).\n$$\n\nIn our case, this gives\n\n$$\ndet(P)=det[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -7 & 4 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot det[\\begin{aligned}8 & 6 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNotice that both matrices are triangular. Therefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P) & =(3\\cdot 1\\cdot (-2))\\cdot (8\\cdot 1\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =(-6)\\cdot (-8) \\\\  & =48.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
